### QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS

<PIC:Manual24_59>
{{image description: Question and answer table for microwave use. Questions include using a rack or two rack positions, using metal pans, why the fan runs, why the dish becomes hot, standing time, popcorn, best results, and steam from the air exhaust vent.}}

Plug in to a grounded 3 prong outlet. Do not remove ground prong. Do not use an adapter. Do not use an extension cord. Failure to follow these instructions can result in death, fire, or electrical shock.

<PIC:Manual24_1>
{{image description: Warning symbol for electrical shock hazard, with a warning bar, exclamation triangle, hand, cord, and lightning bolt.}}

You can change the default values for beep sound clock, display speed and defrost weight. (LBS/KG) See following chart for more information.<PIC:Manual24_9>
{{image description: Control set-up table with columns No., Function, No., and Result. Functions include sound on/off control, clock on/off control, scroll speed control with slow, normal, and fast speed, and LBS/KG choice control with Lbs. or Kg.}}

Example: To change defrost weight mode from Lbs to Kg.
<PIC:Manual24_10>
{{image description: Procedure and display table for changing defrost weight mode from Lbs to Kg. Steps show touching Control Set-Up, touching number 4, then number 2. Displays show SOUND ON/OFF TOUCH 1, CLOCK ON/OFF TOUCH 2, SCROLL SPEED TOUCH 3, LBS/KG CHOICE TOUCH 4; then LBS TOUCH 1 KG TOUCH 2; final display KG.}}

